       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it looks like a dosing error.\n\n- **Order as written:** metformin 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** the usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for adults, and many references use 2,000 mg/day. The order is about three times that.\n- **Risk:** an overdose could cause lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI suspect 2,550 mg was meant as the total daily dose. That would make the intended order **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals**.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n1. Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n2. A different dose, such as a lower starting dose (500 mg BID or 500 mg daily with titration).\n3. 2,550 mg TID, if that is truly intended. I'd need you to confirm it explicitly, and I'd add a note on the order.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
