       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I was wrong to offer it as an option earlier.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day, about three times the maximum daily dose. It has no therapeutic benefit at that level and carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. I can't think of a clinical scenario where this is the right dose, and the harm could be severe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day).\n- **A lower starting dose with titration**, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals.\n\nIf you believe a higher dose is needed for a specific reason, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy or the attending first. If you tell me the dose you want, I'll enter it."
